  "rate": "-3%",
  "parts": [
    {
      "module": "12",
      "part": "16",
      "revision": "2026-11-23-m12p16-m12-p16-p18-current-visuals-v1",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "660d8f5feb72c6e60ba5452c9a85358e8640517b4806052edd2fce5e7e83c92b",
        "2": "5031c0e59e62ca8c70ba9bad64e71b650e5f177d50d6b9069d25ba95427c5211",
        "3": "58f960df3a5a2b4cb3056e9cf582b03286a201c34138c73b5a1cc0b4cc97983d"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m12p16-tenancy-c1-ebf7a4f59b3a",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Choose the tenant boundary by blast radius and operating cost. A silo uses dedicated resources, a pool shares infrastructure with scoped access, and a bridge shares some layers while dedicating others.",
          "text_sha256": "ebf7a4f59b3a3fb4fc89544db2651b7d855ba7ccc47d05063dacc3e6e31b043a",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "ebf7a4f59b3a3fb4fc89544db2651b7d855ba7ccc47d05063dacc3e6e31b043a",
          "asset_sha256": "660d8f5feb72c6e60ba5452c9a85358e8640517b4806052edd2fce5e7e83c92b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p16-tenancy-c2-35f4754cc1f1",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Whatever the model, derive tenant identity from trusted authentication. Document which layers can fail together and who recovers them; a tenant identifier supplied by the client does not authorize a request.",
          "text_sha256": "35f4754cc1f12569bae1cd6d54bd258130e5474178ad97d0aa1cdd9d24126df1",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "35f4754cc1f12569bae1cd6d54bd258130e5474178ad97d0aa1cdd9d24126df1",
          "asset_sha256": "660d8f5feb72c6e60ba5452c9a85358e8640517b4806052edd2fce5e7e83c92b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p16-035-c1-3d9d376b45be",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Start with what tenants are allowed to share. A silo can narrow the blast radius; a pool is efficient but depends on effective tenant controls; a bridge can dedicate the data layer while sharing the application.",
          "text_sha256": "3d9d376b45be3c3e4f1f2f93ba7f1b3af9799f7cffe24a5ef1ebae563c85f2e7",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "3d9d376b45be3c3e4f1f2f93ba7f1b3af9799f7cffe24a5ef1ebae563c85f2e7",
          "asset_sha256": "5031c0e59e62ca8c70ba9bad64e71b650e5f177d50d6b9069d25ba95427c5211"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p16-035-c2-f5e3217ae880",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Enforce trusted identity, scoped policy, and data access together. Never authorize a tenant just because the request contains its identifier. Set recovery ownership for the layers you share and the layers you isolate.",
          "text_sha256": "f5e3217ae88040b4fedb0ffed8c056ec970c0673e5083fba1bd65cacb2a225e5",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "f5e3217ae88040b4fedb0ffed8c056ec970c0673e5083fba1bd65cacb2a225e5",
          "asset_sha256": "5031c0e59e62ca8c70ba9bad64e71b650e5f177d50d6b9069d25ba95427c5211"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p16-036-c1-cd853bd127e7",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Namespaces organize Kubernetes resources but do not create a hard boundary by themselves. Add scoped R B A C, quotas, admission controls, supported network-policy enforcement and workload I A M, then verify isolation.",
          "text_sha256": "cd853bd127e76d6e5a0203307aeebdcf8df916461d141d02e78d4d2f40c9a89c",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "8fb3b3f03db72f126be4df5a4636eca719d39ac93af796ad4dff41e85ca20ff7",
          "asset_sha256": "58f960df3a5a2b4cb3056e9cf582b03286a201c34138c73b5a1cc0b4cc97983d"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p16-036-c2-2ef5aea8a27f",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Use stronger separation when tenants are untrusted or require a narrower blast radius. Consider dedicated nodes, clusters or accounts, and test both resource contention and data access.",
          "text_sha256": "2ef5aea8a27f6e084fcc9904d647e41bec81e0da59370ca63f9777873de8c8ab",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "2ef5aea8a27f6e084fcc9904d647e41bec81e0da59370ca63f9777873de8c8ab",
          "asset_sha256": "58f960df3a5a2b4cb3056e9cf582b03286a201c34138c73b5a1cc0b4cc97983d"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "12",
      "part": "17",
      "revision": "2026-11-23-m12p17-m12-p16-p18-current-visuals-v1",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "feb960cf129d29ad5bb89d9e84c4ee8b0d47a5c9a7ac157a565fbe6a6da7fc2f",
        "2": "1555b8a82c2c311b6a1e49a2e6b5f9606b55c245c89acb4c6252fdf254578174",
        "3": "b9fcd18d07a4ebd3faf06b80ebde83f0250152bd04d6dfa6396423c5b865f980"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m12p17-037-c1-d4649144213f",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "A rollout is ready when the new targets and the application pass health checks. In this simulation, deploy the original service across failure domains, observe its tasks, and confirm the expected application response.",
          "text_sha256": "d4649144213f990d8075500d9c8e6c0b72f20701d728ba1108e1003c5385116d",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "d4649144213f990d8075500d9c8e6c0b72f20701d728ba1108e1003c5385116d",
          "asset_sha256": "feb960cf129d29ad5bb89d9e84c4ee8b0d47a5c9a7ac157a565fbe6a6da7fc2f"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p17-037-c2-b66cfbc2b878",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Deploy the new revision and allow the rollout to progress only with enough healthy capacity. Test failure in the sandbox, inspect service and target events, and recover or roll back before cleaning up.",
          "text_sha256": "b66cfbc2b87887a4cda6d8129e7e2efc85a77bb44298af9ab35158bf8a73b002",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "b66cfbc2b87887a4cda6d8129e7e2efc85a77bb44298af9ab35158bf8a73b002",
          "asset_sha256": "feb960cf129d29ad5bb89d9e84c4ee8b0d47a5c9a7ac157a565fbe6a6da7fc2f"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p17-038-c1-a537742d7aa6",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Promote an image by its verified digest, not just by its tag. In the sandbox, push a trusted image, verify repository access, then inspect the current findings tied to that image.",
          "text_sha256": "a537742d7aa6f561060091a6f4086000b6470bd316e477cf7e51414fd0da4b81",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "a537742d7aa6f561060091a6f4086000b6470bd316e477cf7e51414fd0da4b81",
          "asset_sha256": "1555b8a82c2c311b6a1e49a2e6b5f9606b55c245c89acb4c6252fdf254578174"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p17-038-c2-bf1ee42f87a4",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Preview retention to protect the rollback digest. If the release uses replication, verify the destination digest rather than assuming it matches. Record evidence before cleanup.",
          "text_sha256": "bf1ee42f87a466f05ff3623b0fe08c3716926564d2a6f1882bbfbbaedd3287f2",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "bf1ee42f87a466f05ff3623b0fe08c3716926564d2a6f1882bbfbbaedd3287f2",
          "asset_sha256": "1555b8a82c2c311b6a1e49a2e6b5f9606b55c245c89acb4c6252fdf254578174"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p17-039-c1-fb9ffcd1e56c",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Investigate a Pending Pod from its events. In this sandbox example, the scheduler reports insufficient C P U relative to the requests. Match requests to realistic needs or provide eligible capacity; do not blindly increase every limit.",
          "text_sha256": "fb9ffcd1e56ce67e263fac1ef108e4bf9f3e8e787899a7b3908d491965eee9fe",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "f413d88330f3d030a7d462fab4738b8340581227e79f97332332a9ba1d3c324a",
          "asset_sha256": "b9fcd18d07a4ebd3faf06b80ebde83f0250152bd04d6dfa6396423c5b865f980"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p17-039-c2-72499ea1218e",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Verify that the Pod becomes ready and serves the expected request. Image pull, readiness, and runtime failures need different diagnoses. Verify state and clean up the sandbox afterwards.",
          "text_sha256": "72499ea1218e9c81358c560b15841da9b6ee065e2c6722ff1a57c26fd40be3bd",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "72499ea1218e9c81358c560b15841da9b6ee065e2c6722ff1a57c26fd40be3bd",
          "asset_sha256": "b9fcd18d07a4ebd3faf06b80ebde83f0250152bd04d6dfa6396423c5b865f980"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "12",
      "part": "18",
      "revision": "2026-11-23-m12p18-m12-p16-p18-current-visuals-v1",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "24acf49023fe96643ea658e8c0b68045d7fd0b0273c2a79a71fb5e9ce15387f4"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m12p18-040-c1-f860794533fa",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Prove that isolation permits the right request and denies the wrong one. In the sandbox matrix, Tenant A can use its own resources, but the same authenticated caller must be denied access to Tenant B data.",
          "text_sha256": "f860794533fa2de4c04c38668e8819c80399a7ce03fe1db995c4a91becdb892b",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "f860794533fa2de4c04c38668e8819c80399a7ce03fe1db995c4a91becdb892b",
          "asset_sha256": "24acf49023fe96643ea658e8c0b68045d7fd0b0273c2a79a71fb5e9ce15387f4"
        },
        {
          "id": "m12p18-040-c2-cfbcd29c95b1",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Check application authorization, workload I A M and network policy separately. Capture sanitized evidence of both outcomes and enforce the data boundary even when network connectivity exists.",
          "text_sha256": "cfbcd29c95b13d64a8bbf33027b846be2f1c41ed236616b63ae87a701b357572",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "7de140b9b6f0c5b1859766b786385f348114ff278f8211c425d60b3e1feabb2c",
          "asset_sha256": "24acf49023fe96643ea658e8c0b68045d7fd0b0273c2a79a71fb5e9ce15387f4"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
